# Generated by agent-harness (sync_harnesses.py) from .claude/. Anchored with a
# leading slash so they match only at the repo root.
#
# NOT stowed onto this workstation: ~/.codex/skills is a real directory holding
# separately installed skills, so linking this one over it makes `stow -R .`
# fail with a conflict. Coder workspaces get them instead, via a start script
# that writes its own ignore list — see apps/coder/manifests/template/main.tf
# in inkfish-cluster.
^/\.agents$
^/\.codex$
^/\.openhands$

# Repo conventions, not machine config. Stowed to ~/AGENTS.md it would be picked
# up as a parent-directory instructions file by agents working anywhere under $HOME.
^/AGENTS\.md$
# Repo-internal git metadata. Stow would link it to ~/.gitmodules, where it is
# meaningless -- git only reads .gitmodules at a repo root.
^/\.gitmodules$

# Not recognised by GNU stow -- only .stow-local-ignore (package) and
# ~/.stow-global-ignore are. Left in the repo but kept out of $HOME, where they
# were being stowed as inert junk symlinks.
^/\.stow-ignore$
^/\.stowignore$

# Per-host package. Stowed explicitly on the Mac: stow -d ~/dotfiles -t ~ mac
# (anchored so it cannot prune an unrelated directory named "mac" deeper in the tree)
^/mac$

# chezmoi's territory. stow must never touch these: chezmoi writes real files
# and would fight stow's symlinks over any shared path.
^/chezmoi$
^/\.chezmoiroot$
